  "verbalization": "Pembrolizumab, a monoclonal antibody, is associated with Lung Cancer through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Pembrolizumab is indicated for Lung Cancer, which in turn is linked to Non-small Cell Lung Carcinoma (NSCLC) via multiple indications. Specifically, Pembrolizumab is indicated for Lung Cancer, and this condition is indicated for Alectinib, Olmutinib, and Necitumumab, all of which are indicated for NSCLC. This creates a chain of indications that connects Pembrolizumab to NSCLC through the disease itself. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Lung Cancer as a central node in the relationship between Pembrolizumab and NSCLC, emphasizing the importance of the disease in mediating the drug's effect. The evidence supports a mechanism where Pembrolizumab is indirectly linked to NSCLC via its indications, with the disease serving as a critical intermediary.",
